    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνσκέλλω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνισκ-</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dry</i> or <i>wither up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τοι ένισκήλη . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					694
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, with pf.
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέσκληκα,</span>
			<i>to be dry, withered,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				1.28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνεσκληκὼς γὰρ ἀνίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.166
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i>): also of timber, <i>to be dry, seasoned,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1251
			</span></i>.</div>
